(c) binary IFS {x->2x, x->2x+1} from 1 = the integers (binary tree); AP = truncation
    doubling map x->2x mod n on {1..n-1}: orbit of 1, and order/degeneracy
   n= 7: orbit of 1 under x->2x mod n: [1, 2, 4, 1]; ord_2(mod 7)=3
   n=13: orbit of 1 under x->2x mod n: [1, 2, 4, 8, 3, 6, 12, 11, 9, 5, 10, 7, 1]; ord_2(mod 13)=12
   n=14: orbit of 1 under x->2x mod n: [1, 2, 4, 8, 2]; 2 NOT invertible mod 14 (degenerate doubling)
   n=16: orbit of 1 under x->2x mod n: [1, 2, 4, 8, 0]; 2 NOT invertible mod 16 (degenerate doubling)
